One Week in the Jurassic — an Art Deco film (11 min)

Script and voiceover: supplied by the user (recorded with ElevenLabs, voice "Peter – Youthful and Expressive").
The voice is used as supplied; the film only levels it.

Picture: everything drawn in code (Canvas2D), no generated images, no third-party artwork.
Dinosaurs are drawn from published skeletal proportions (body length, hip height, limb ratios, skull shape).
Drawing engine adapted from the library's Art Deco style tools.

Map data: Natural Earth 1:50m land polygons (public domain), coastline only, no borders drawn.
  https://www.naturalearthdata.com/
The Morrison Formation outline and state label positions are approximate, drawn by hand.

